{
  "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
  "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
  "model": "HV305 HVAC micro drive (MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "hv305",
  "short_model": "HV305",
  "aliases": [
    "HV35U",
    "HV305 drive",
    "HV305 Versatile Compact Drive"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Yaskawa HV305 drives using the built-in RS-485 port with H5-08 = 0 (MEMOBUS/Modbus), per technical reference SIEPYAIHV3001B.",
  "summary": "Yaskawa's compact HVAC drive with a built-in RS-485 port that runs MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU or BACnet MS/TP. Command registers (run bits, frequency reference, PID setpoint, outputs) start at 0001H, status and monitor registers at 0020H, and every parameter is reachable at the hex number printed under it. This map covers the command and status words, key monitors, fault bits and the b1/H5 setup parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 31,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Register numbers are hex and are sent unchanged: the manual's read example (Figure 6.9) asks slave 2 for starting register 0020H as bytes 00 20. Parameters use the hex number printed under each parameter (H5-01 = 0425H)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "HV305 Drive Technical Reference",
    "doc_number": "SIEPYAIHV3001B",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=SIEPYAIHV3001&cmd=documents&documentName=SIEPYAIHV3001.pdf",
    "pages": "Section 6.3 MEMOBUS/Modbus: Table 6.2 specs, Table 6.5 function codes p. 230, Figure 6.9 read example p. 231, Table 6.11 command data pp. 237-239, Table 6.12 monitor data pp. 240-245; b1/H5 parameter tables in chapter 11 (H5 pp. 438-440)."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Frequency registers 0002H, 0023H and 0024H use the units chosen in o1-03, so they are left unscaled.",
    "Left out: 0007H analog output setting, 000AH pulse output, 0025H output voltage (unit switched by H5-10), 0026H output current, 0027H output power and 0028H/0032H torque reference (unit/sign not fixed for every model), 002FH frequency reference bias, 003EH/003FH output frequency in r/min or 0.01 % (sign not stated), the U-monitor and fault-history blocks from 0040H, 15C0H extended inputs and the clock registers 3004H-3007H.",
    "Supported function codes are 03H, 08H, 10H, 5AH and 67H (non-consecutive read/write); there is no 06H, so use 10H even for a single register.",
    "U4-01 cumulative operation time is split over two 16-bit registers (0098H = value / 10, 0099H = last digit), not a 32-bit value.",
    "H5-11 defaults to 1 (Enter not required) on this drive; with H5-11 = 0, parameter writes need the Enter command (0900H or 0910H).",
    "Stop bits are set by H5-29 (3AB0H): 1 or 2, default 1."
  ],
